{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"stripe config --help | sed -n '1,200p'; printf '\\\\nStripe config files:\\\\n'; find /Users/mchl/.config/stripe -maxdepth 2 -type f -print 2>/dev/null | sort; printf '\\\\nKey fields present:\\\\n'; rg -n 'secret|publish|api_key|key' /Users/mchl/.config/stripe 2>/dev/null | sed -E 's/(= *).*/\\\\1[redacted]/' || true\"","aggregated_output":"config lets you set and unset specific configuration values for your profile if\nyou need more granular control over the configuration.\n\nUsage:\n  stripe config [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  stripe config --list\n  stripe config --set color off\n  stripe config --unset color\n  stripe config --remove-profile my-project\n\n[Agent guidance]\n  If you do not have an account: run stripe sandbox create (provisions a claimable sandbox without a browser).\n  If you already have a key: use --api-key (or set STRIPE_API_KEY).\n  Run stripe --map to quickly see all available commands.\n  Run stripe resources to discover all available API resources.\n  Run stripe [resource] --help to see operations and required/common parameters for a resource.\n  Run stripe help [resource] [operation] to see the full parameter list for a specific operation.\n\n\nFlags:\n  -c, --confirm                 Skip the confirmation prompt for\n                                --remove-profile\n  -e, --edit                    Open an editor to the config file\n  -h, --help                    help for config\n      --list                    List configs\n      --remove-profile string   Remove a profile and its stored\n                                credentials from the config file\n      --set                     Set a config field to some value\n      --unset string            Unset a specific config field\n\nGlobal flags:\n      --api-key string        Your API key to use for the command\n      --color string          turn on/off color output (on, off, auto)\n      --co